[4301.586796, "i", "sed -n '1,120p' README.md\n"]
[4301.587109, "o", "sed -n '1,120p' README.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4301.590415, "o", "# Nexus - ML Model & Experiment Management\r\n\r\nNexus is a command-line tool for managing ML models, experiments, and datasets.\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n- **Model Registry**: Register, version, and manage ML model lifecycle\r\n- **Experiment Tracking**: Create experiments, log metrics and parameters\r\n- **Dataset Catalog**: Track dataset versions and metadata\r\n- **Tag-based Search**: Find entities across the registry using tags\r\n\r\n## Usage\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Model management\r\n"]
[4301.590583, "o", "nexus model register my-model --version 1.0.0 --framework tensorflow\r\nnexus model list\r\nnexus model promote my-model 1.0.0 production\r\n\r\n# Experiment tracking\r\nnexus experiment create training-run-1 --params lr=0.001,epochs=100\r\nnexus experiment log-metric exp-0001 accuracy 0.95\r\nnexus experiment complete exp-0001\r\n\r\n# Dataset management\r\nnexus dataset register my-dataset 1.0 csv /data/train.csv --rows 10000\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Architecture\r\n\r\nData is stored as JSON in `/tmp/nexus/`. The storage layer provides thread-safe\r\nread/write access with atomic file operations (write-to-temp then rename).\r\n\r\nModels follow a lifecycle: registered -> staging -> production -> archived.\r\nOnly one model version per name can be in production at a time; promoting a new\r\nversion auto-demotes the previous production version to staging.\r\n\r\nExperiments can reference models and datasets for lineage tracking. The store\r\nenforces referential integrity: you cannot delete a model that is referenced by\r\nan experiment, and you cannot create an "]
[4301.590686, "o", "experiment referencing a non-existent\r\nmodel or dataset.\r\n\r\nTags are indexed globally across all entity types (models, experiments). A tag\r\nsearch returns keys from any entity type that carries that tag.\r\n"]
[4301.591079, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[4301.591149, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[4301.866832, "i", "grep -n \"func main\\|os.Args\\|Command\\|run\\|dry-run\\|pipeline\" main.go\n"]
